<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census. [CORRECTED 02:00 GMT 28/3]</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census. [CORRECTED 02:00 GMT 28/3]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,289.1 million lbs of vegoils in February in edible product output versus a revised 1,347.8 million lbs in January and 1,156.9 in February 1996.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --    Feb 97   Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil   1,026.0   1,121.0     959.6</p>
<p>(Corrects Feb 97 soybean oil with refining losses from 2,147.0 and Feb 96 from 1,958.8)</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1997	   1996</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil   1,026.0	  959.6</p>
<p>(Corrects figures as above)</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude   2,823.2	2,597.0</p>
<p>		     Refined   1,896.0	1,914.2</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude     238.6	  252.3</p>
<p>		     Refined     167.3	  176.3</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude     343.3	  341.1</p>
<p>		     Refined     131.4	  160.7</p>
</text>
